+# Aegis Quickwins: Cloud / Edge / IoT / Quantum
+
+This patch implements practical starter pieces to improve Aegis across cloud, edge, IoT and quantum domains:
+
+- CI pre-deploy verification (.github/workflows/verify_mcp_cosign.yml) to check MCP JSON cosign signatures.
+- Postgres backup CronJob template for MCP (helm/mcp/templates/postgres-backup-cronjob.yaml).
+- ONNX -> TensorRT helper (scripts/push_onnx_to_trt.py) and k3s edge install playbook (edge/k3s/install_k3s_edge.sh).
+- Triton helm edge tweaks already available; push_onnx_to_trt helps prepare model repo.
+- Lightweight MQTT edge agent (iot/mqtt_agent.py) that uploads pointers to S3 and posts MCP-lite metadata to MCP.
+- Quantum-runner example service (quantum/quantum_runner) using Qiskit simulator that records results to MCP.
+
+Notes:
+- These are starter implementations — adapt for production by adding robust auth, retries, batching, and device attestation.
+- Ensure secrets (AWS, COSIGN_PUB, AEGIS_MCP_API) are configured in your environment or GitHub Secrets.
